<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope John XIX</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1032</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Romanus of Tusculum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope John XIX, born Romanus, was pope from 1024 to 1032, a member of the family of the counts of Tusculum. A layman, he succeeded his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-benedict-viii">Benedict VIII</a> and received all holy orders in a single day. He crowned Conrad II emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1027.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-john-xix.jpg" alt="Pope John XIX" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bari_Exultet_roll_1_-_emperors_and_pope_(pope1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
